Z||000015||4UMLA1||11-27-2001||10:30 PM||||Well, I guess I might as well stick my 2 cents in on this one.  I hate NASCAR, I really dont see the purpose of driving around in a circle for 3 hours, is that racing?  How hard is it to set up a car for driving around in a circle at 200 mph?  It seams like all it would take is a lot of downforce, stiff springs and the car as low as it will go, oh, and a lot of camber.  How hard is that to do?  I just don't understand it.<BR>Now if you want to see some real racing, go to the Formula 1 race at Indy. next year, that is real racing.  Formula 1 is the greatest racing sport in the world.  They dont run on ovals, all of there races are done on road courses all around the world.  It is more of a challenge to set up cars for road courses than just driving around in a circle <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||12
