Z||000023||WKDFIRO||11-28-2001||09:51 AM||||I like NASCAR, I also love GT3 racing. I really like all forms of motor racing.  I don't have cable so I don't see a lot of Formula 1 racing, (if I had Speedvision, I wouldn't leave the house...mmmmmm.....racing....mmmmmmmmm.) but I do love the contradiction in 4UMLA 1's post. <P>So a bunch of red necks hicks go around in circles for 3 hours at the Brickyard 400(is it 400?) isn't racing but a bunch of stuck up eurotrash in Formula 1 at the same track IS racing?<P>Ok.<P>I used to go to the Long Beach Grand Prix until I realized how bored I was. Road courses are more fun on TV but oval racing is fun because of the passing, bumping and grinding. You just don't trade paint in Cart or Formula 1 without getting expensive. I would imagine you see a lot more passing in an oval track weather its Formula or NASCAR and that makes for a great race. Thats why Indy is so famous.||||reg||6
