Z||000025||ITB 2M4||11-28-2001||03:04 PM||||I think a lot of you guys would be suprised at how much technology there really is in NASCAR.  My cousin graduated from Univ. of Tx. with a marketing degree, and went to work for the Jasper Engines team of Robert Pressley, so I've had an opportunity to see the cars (not the show cars either) up close.<P>I run in the Sports Car Club of America's Improved Touring B class with my '84 Fiero.  There's not a car that can touch it in the corners because of all the chassis work done by a guy that hasn't run in NASCAR since the early 70's.  He put a quick set-up on the car before I went to the infield road course at Daytona, and then a race at Sebring.  He didn't have any tire temps to go by, or my input, cause I hadn't driven the car at that point yet.  I told him Fiero's naturally push, and he gave me a set-up that has just the slightest hint of oversteer.  The car is perfectly balanced, and I can outrun cars that have more motor than me just because I can get through the corners so much quicker.  When my dad's '74 Corolla SR-5 got crunched, he took the spare body we had, chopped both cars in half, and welded the back half of the race car to the good front half of the parts car.  The car went a second and a half quicker despite the new motor making less hp!<P>I suggest you go to Mooresville, N.C. where most of the NASCAR shops are located, and take a look around.  Go during the week (Tues.-Thurs.), cause they are almost always gone to the races Fri.-Mon.  Ask some questions of the guys in the shops.  One of the guys at Ricky Rudds' shop told me quite a bit about the cars.<P>P.S.- Ford brought in the Woods Brothers NASCAR team to help them win the Indy 500, because the NASCAR guys had figured out how to make really fast pit stops.  The 'intellectuals' at the 500 hadn't figured out that every second in the pit cost about 300ft. on the race track yet.<P>------------------<BR>SCCA ITB '84 Fiero 2M4||||reg||1
Z||000026||thomas_l||11-28-2001||04:29 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by My7Fieros:<BR><B><BR>Ditto. If I wanted to watch a bunch of rednecks drive 500 miles in a circle, I'd sit on the I-240 loop that circles Memphis!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> (No offense to anyone)<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I thought that would be the Craftsman Truck Series up there not Winston Cup   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> j/k<P>Sounds more like some of the folks circling the parking lot after lunch where I work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by thomas_l (edited 11-28-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000027||mrfixit58||11-28-2001||04:42 PM||||I wasn't going to comment because this topic should really be discussed in the O/T section. But, since there is a picture of a Fiero with *gag* Gordon colors posted I'll throw in my 2-cents worth:<P>1) I have all my own teeth still in my head and like(ed) NASCAR. I have attended every Daytona 500 from 1985 through 2001.<P>2) I've lost a lot of interest because all the cars are so regulated that they now all look too much alike. They might as well be IROC cars.<P>3) For those who think turning left at 200 MPH for 500 miles isn't racing and CART and Indy is... give me the name of other race car driver from the other types of racing who have won the IROC series ... besides the NASCAR guys (I can think of only a few and only one in what is considered the modern era).<P>4) One could make a strong argument that NHRA is even less "racing" than NASCAR. Heck, they don't even turn left. Of course, if your man (or woman) enough to strap a controlled explosion to your butt and accelerated it to over 300 MPH in 1/4 mile, you can call it anything you want.<P>5) Big E was to NASCAR as Michael Jordan is to the NBA... magical. It's all about attitude. If you could clone only one driver to race NASCAR it would be Dale. Regardless of how many of his records will be broken, Dale legacy and legend will live on.<P>I'm done,<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy  :D <BR>Just another stock Blue 87 GT   <BR>Suncoast Fieros<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG">          <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <P><B>JUST ADDED: </B>1988 GT w/ T-Tops, 5-Speed, and Performance Sound.||||reg||6
Z||000028||Formula88||11-28-2001||05:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>Hey smooth (xlax) gt, a bunch of people here are insulting (telling the truth about) your precious nascar, and you don't say a thing, but when I do it you burst a blood vessel.  Do you only confront me because you feel the need to have the forums support, because I happen to drive a different kinda car?  Pathetic.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Maybe it's because you're a jerk?  Dunno, just a thought.  Most people here (i.e. who aren't you) can state their opinions and disagree with someone without trying to attack or belittle the person with differing views. ||||reg||1
